    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d306">

                <pb facs="0479" n="355" xml:id="pg355"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3585: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-11-19T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 19,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 19—9:30
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>409. My 403, November 16th, noon [<hi rendition="#italic">midnight</hi>].
                    Continue, payments by the two banks virtually ceased, governmental agencies
                    still accepting notes. Hsu Un Yan [<hi rendition="#italic">Hsu
                        En-yuan?</hi><anchor n="32" xml:id="d306-f1"/>] informs me this is the most
                    severe panic on record. All silver has disappeared from circulation, business at
                    a standstill, Cabinet discussing moratorium.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d306-f1" n="32" xml:id="d306-f1-content">
                <p>Vice President of the Chinese American Bank of Commerce.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
